# Container builds no stock-pull.sh pre-pull can reach (doppler#1982).
# Read by scripts/check_stock_images.py (make lint-stock-images, #1979).
#
# A build that runs `docker/setup-buildx-action` uses the docker-container
# driver, which runs BuildKit in its own container: it resolves and pulls the
# FROMs there, so an image pulled into the runner's daemon is never
# consulted, and BuildKit does not retry a 429.
#
# EMPTY since #1982, and meant to stay so. Every such build here now pulls
# from a registry a probe chose under retry: release.yml's images through
# `make stock-registry` (#2572), the CI-image rebuild through canonical's
# `make ci-image-base` (just-buildit.github.io#139). A new one is wired the
# same way, not listed here.
#
# One site per line: the workflow, then the Dockerfile (with `:target` when
# the step builds one), then why. This list may only SHRINK: the gate fails
# on an entry that no longer names a container-driver build, on a new
# container-driver build that is not listed, and on an entry the list did
# not have at the merge base with origin/main, so listing a new build is
# not a way in. Fix the build instead (#1982).
